Fan review complete and saved to `docs/content-analysis/perspective-reviews/Noah-Wyle/2026-08-09_020207/fan.md` (SHA verified against context.json and the supplied argument before reading).

**Verdict:** trust strained, value high, delight clear_hit — **recommendation: revise**. The writer genuinely understood Wyle; the problems are currency and small canon wobbles, all fixable from the existing evidence packet without new research.

**Blockers: 1.** The draft says Wyle "submitted himself for acting and directing both" — but he was *nominated* for both (Lead Actor + Outstanding Directing for "12:00 P.M.") on July 8, 2026, per the packet's Tier 1 Television Academy source. The same paragraph cites the 25 nominations from that very announcement, so the line is both stale and internally inconsistent — and it understates the exact fact fans celebrated loudest this year.

**Strongest hit:** the cold-open reframe — "on the biggest night of his career he dressed in her uniform and gave his trophy to her colleagues" — connecting the FIGS scrubs tuxedo fans already knew about to his nurse mother, with the drawer dialogue and "Somewhere" ending as the untouchable spine.

**Highest-priority concern (of 8):** the missed Carter-intervention mirror (FAN-C8). The draft cites Carter's addiction arc and Abbot's finale intervention of Robby in separate sections and never connects them, even though press already frames Robby's arc against Carter's and the piece's own "Carter with the idealism burned off" line sets up the rhyme. Two sentences would add the single most shareable insight for ER-era fans. Other notable concerns: the phone ban was John Wells's policy, not Wyle's; the lawsuit is breach of contract, not "a copyright case"; and the Capitol trip was June 2025, not "Spring."

Sources: [MovieWeb — ER vs. The Pitt's Robby problem](https://movieweb.com/er-fixed-the-pitt-season-2-robby-problem/), [The TV Cave — S2 finale recap](https://www.thetvcave.com/post/the-pitt-season-2-finale-recap), [Time — S2 finale](https://time.com/article/2026/04/10/the-pitt-season-2-finale-robby/), [Gold Derby — finale showrunner interview](https://www.goldderby.com/tv/2026/the-pitt-recap-season-2-episode-15-finale-spoiler-interview/), [Wikipedia — Noah Wyle](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noah_Wyle)
